{% if doc_form == 'catalog' %}
The spec is the `{{ spec_path }}/` directory, one file per section (`NN-slug.md`, the file number is the section number "§N"); the list of sections is `{{ spec_path }}/README.md`. Sections hold folded requirements with version marks "(1.N)". The revision journal is `{{ revisions_path }}/`, one file per revision: what changed and why. Revisions not yet folded into sections are printed by `knowledge/spec-unfolded.sh` (the same list is in the spec README): for them the revision file is normative, not the section. Nobody reads the whole spec: the needed section is found by file name and headings (`grep -n '^#' {{ spec_path }}/*.md`).
{% else %}
The spec is the file `{{ spec_path }}`, the revision journal is `{{ revisions_path }}`: what changed and why, one section per version. The folded part of the spec carries the current requirements with version marks "(1.N)". Revisions not yet folded into it are listed in the spec header: for them the journal section is normative. Nobody reads whole files: the needed paragraph is found by headings (`grep -n '^## \|^### ' {{ spec_path }} {{ revisions_path }}`) and read as a line range.
{% endif %}
